VERDICT: APPROVED
The changes correctly implement the stated task: slides are no longer edge-to-edge, and index math has been consistently updated to the new slide interval.

Critical findings / analysis:
- The pager behavior was transitioned from `pagingEnabled` to `snapToInterval` using a shared interval of `SW + ITEM_SPACING`, which is the right mechanism for introducing inter-slide spacing.
- Slide layout is internally consistent: item container width, `getItemLayout`, and settled-index calculation all use the same widened item width. This avoids drift and off-by-one issues after swipes.
- Media content (image/video) remains `SW` wide while each cell is wider, producing the intended visible black gap between slides without changing core media rendering behavior.
- No evidence of regressions in navigation, initial index positioning, or active-item tracking from this diff.

Security: none observed.

Next actions:
1) Mark task complete.
2) Optionally do a quick device check on iOS + Android to confirm snap feel and last-item snapping are acceptable UX with the new interval.

